"/us/en/foot-and-ankle/products/osteotomy-truss-system": {"template":"product-detail","metadata":{"title":"Osteotomy Truss System","pageTitle":"Osteotomy Truss System","description":"The Osteotomy Truss System™ has an Advanced Structural Design that incorporates 4WEB Medical’s proprietary Truss Implant Technology™. Under normal loading conditions the struts in the truss implant transfer strain to adjacent cellular material which stimulates a mechanobiologic response.1-3","image":null,"imageAlt":null,"tags":["stryker:product/foot-and-ankle","stryker:specialty/foot-&-ankle","stryker:content-type/product","stryker:procedure/foot-and-ankle/opening-wedge-osteotomy/wedges","stryker:procedure/foot-and-ankle/medial-cuneiform-dorsal-opening-wedge-(cotton)-osteotomy/wedges","stryker:business-unit/foot-and-ankle","stryker:specialty/hindfoot","stryker:portfolio/orthopaedics","stryker:procedure/foot-and-ankle/lateral-column-lengthening-(evans-osteotomy)/wedges","stryker:specialty/forefoot","stryker:specialty/midfoot","stryker:content-type/hcp_content","stryker:capability/foot-and-ankle"],"originallyPublished":"2026-01-09T15:25:33.000Z","lastPublished":"2026-01-09T15:35:21.000Z","contentID":"FA-4WEB-SYK-2572700_REV-0_en_us"},"anchors":[{"id":"about","title":"About","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"specification","title":"Specification","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"resources","title":"Resources","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"contact","title":"Contact","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"}],"disclaimer":"<p><b>References</b></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Caffrey, et al, Journal of Biomechanics, 49 (2016) 4090-4097.</li>\r\n<li>Ganey, Journal of the Spinal Research Foundation, 8 (2013) 45-48.</li>\r\n<li>Kiapour A., et al. Bone Mineralization and Spinal Fusion Evaluation of a Truss-based Interbody Fusion Device. Spine Vol. 47, Number 7, pp E319-E327. 2021.</li>\r\n<li>He SJ, Kiapour A, et al. Engineered Hierarchical Surface Roughness Regulates Mesenchymal Stem Cell Spreading, Proliferation, and Differentiation on Titanium Implants. OR$ 2022, Poster No. 1254</li>\r\n<li>Xin X, Radcliff K, et al. Titanium Implants Manufactured with Proprietary 3D-Printing Build Themes Contain Surface Features that Increase Biologic Activity, SMISS 2019. https://broadwater.com/smiss2019/abstracts/#page=52.<br>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Data on file: Collino RR, Begley BR. The effect of contact topology on indentation and implications for subsidence in bone.</li>\r\n<li><a href=\"https://4webmedical.com/technology/\">https://4webmedical.com/technology/</a></li>\r\n</ol>","forms":[{"formId":"3079","afterSubmitAction":"showMessage","message":"Thank you!","useProduction":true}],"tabs":[],"cardLists":[],"missingAlt":["/content/dam/stryker/foot-and-ankle/images/header_forefoot.jpg","/content/dam/stryker/foot-and-ankle/images/Header_Hindfoot.jpg","/content/dam/stryker/foot-and-ankle/images/header_midfoot.jpg"]},
