"/us/en/surgical-technologies/products/neptune-waste-management-system": {"template":"product-detail","metadata":{"title":"Neptune 3 ","pageTitle":"Neptune 3","description":"Neptune 3 is a constantly closed fluid, smoke, and aerosol filtration system that comes with standard integration of HEPA and ULPA filtration.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/surgical-technologies/products/neptune-3/images/neptune3-plus-hero-v2.png","imageAlt":"Neptune 3","tags":["stryker:content-type/product","stryker:services/procare/surgical/surgical-suction","stryker:portfolio/medical-and-surgical-equipment","stryker:capability/surgical-suction","stryker:capability/covid-19-products","stryker:specialty/fluid-waste-management","stryker:business-unit/surgical_technologies","stryker:content-type/hcp_content","stryker:product/surgical_technologies/Neptune_3"],"originallyPublished":"2023-02-06T13:04:51.000Z","lastPublished":"2026-06-09T19:08:47.000Z","contentID":"ST-GSNPS-OTHD-2265338_REV-0"},"anchors":[{"id":"contact","title":"Contact","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"}],"disclaimer":"<p>*Zero splash and spills, zero airborne contaminants, zero smoke, zero retained surgical sponges, zero blind spots, zero trips &amp; falls, zero drug diversion, and zero doubt messages are not guarantees and are aspirational in nature.</p>\r\n<p>Instructions for use: <a href=\"https://labeling.stryker.com/hcp/US\">https://labeling.stryker.com/hcp/US</a></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>“Updated U.S. Public Health Service Guidelines for the Management of Occupational Exposures to HBV, HCV, and HIV and Recommendations for Postexposure Prophylaxis.” 29 June 2001, www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/rr5011a1.htm.”</li>\r\n<li>Horn, Martlie et al. “Traditional canister-based open waste management system versus closed system: hazardous exposure prevention and operating theatre staff satisfaction.” Journal of Perioperative Nursing in Australia. 28:1 (Autumn 2015):18-22.</li>\r\n<li>Boyd HR, Stanley C. Sources of error when tracking irrigation fluids during hysteroscopic procedures. J Am Assoc Gynecol Laparosc. 2000;7(4):472-476.</li>\r\n<li>Stryker data on file; S1756.071362, S1756.071444, S1756.071469, S1756.071450, S1988.150724.</li>\r\n<li>Baker S, Clark J, Pla AB, Feixas EV, Huegel J, Tariq L. Neptune versus canister-based surgical waste management in Europe: results of the GREEN study. Ann Med Surg (Lond). 2023 Jul 31;85(9):4307-4314. doi: 10.1097/MS9.0000000000000934.</li>\r\n<li>BT-0000088552, Neptune3 DIOVV, AF D20.10 states small canister shall hold 4 +/- 0.5 L and D20.15 states large canister shall hold 20+/-0.5 L</li>\r\n<li>Pierce JS, Lacey SE, Lippert JF, Lopez R, Franke JE. Laser-generated air contaminants from medical laser applications: a state-of-the-science review of exposure characterization, health</li>\r\n<li>Andreasson S, Mahteme H, Sahlberg B, Anundi H. Polycyclic Aromatic Hydrocarbons in Electrocautery Smoke during Peritonectomy Procedures. Journal of Environmental and Public Health. 2012: 1-6.</li>\r\n</ol>","forms":[{"formId":"3248","afterSubmitAction":"showMessage","message":"Thank you!","useProduction":true}],"tabs":[["Product information","Related products"]],"cardLists":[{"component":"featuredcontent_copy","title":null,"items":[{"path":"/us/en/surgical-technologies/products/cactus-controlled-substance-waste-management-system","resolved":true,"title":"Cactus","description":"A better solution for disposing controlled substance waste.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/surgical-technologies/products/cactus/images/Cactus header 2.png","alt":"Cactus thumbnail"},{"path":"/us/en/surgical-technologies/products/safeair-compact-evacuator","resolved":false}]}],"missingAlt":[]},
"/us/en/surgical-technologies/products/photonblade-3-se": {"template":"product-detail","metadata":{"title":"PhotonBlade 3 SE","pageTitle":null,"description":null,"image":"/content/dam/stryker/surgical-technologies/products/photonblade3/images/PhotonBlade 3 SE header.png","imageAlt":"Photonblade3SE -product","tags":["stryker:specialty/Illuminated_Suction","stryker:capability/plastic-surgery","stryker:capability/reconstructive-surgery","stryker:specialty/breast","stryker:business-unit/surgical_technologies","stryker:capability/Illuminated_instruments","stryker:content-type/hcp_content","stryker:capability/surgical-visualization","stryker:content-type/product","stryker:portfolio/medical-and-surgical-equipment","stryker:specialty/surgical-smoke-evacuation","stryker:capability/surgical-suction","stryker:specialty/Illuminated_Advanced_Energy","stryker:specialty/plastic-surgery"],"originallyPublished":"2026-06-08T16:16:29.000Z","lastPublished":"2026-06-08T16:16:29.000Z","contentID":"ST-PB3-MICRO-1718284_REV-0"},"anchors":[{"id":"overview","title":"Overview","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"features","title":"Features","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"resources","title":"Resources","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"contact","title":"Contact Us","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"}],"disclaimer":"<p>*Zero splash and spills, zero airborne contaminants, zero smoke, zero retained surgical sponges, zero blind spots, zero trips &amp; falls, zero drug diversion, and zero doubt messages are not guarantees and are aspirational in nature.</p>\r\n<p>† PhotonBlade 3 does not offer smoke evacuation capabilities.</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Canicoba ARB. Surgical smoke and occupational health. Ann Transl Med. 2022 Dec;10(24):1303. doi: 10.21037/atm-22-5631. PMID: 36660725; PMCID: PMC9843373.</li>\r\n<li>In a blinded study of 17 surgeons, PhotonBlade 3 SE smoke evacuation integration and performance rated an average of 4.8 out of 5. Data on file.</li>\r\n<li>Evidence: Engineering Test Report: 2401515-01 Rev A. When compared to PlasmaBlade x3 Light, testing date October 2-4, 2024.</li>\r\n<li>In a blinded survey of 17 surgeons, PhotonBlade 3 SE thermal spread and surrounding tissue damage was rated an average of 4.5 out of 5. Data on file.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>An average of 97% smoke removal was noted in engineering testing when connected to Stryker Compact Smoke Evacuation Unit and the Stryker Neptune Waste Management System. Data on File.</li>\r\n<li>Data on file. Engineering Test Report: Test Report S12086.240769 (with Neptune) , Test Report S12086.240696 (with Compact), Polaris test report S2579.232113, and HFE report (D0000300823).</li>\r\n</ol>","forms":[{"formId":"3248","afterSubmitAction":"showMessage","message":"Thank you!","useProduction":true}],"tabs":[["PhotonBlade 3 SE","PhotonBlade 3†"],["Product information","Related products"]],"cardLists":[{"component":"featuredcontent","title":null,"items":[{"path":"/us/en/surgical-technologies/products/safeair-compact-evacuator","resolved":false},{"path":"/us/en/surgical-technologies/products/neptune-waste-management-system","resolved":true,"title":"Neptune 3 ","description":"Neptune 3 is a constantly closed fluid, smoke, and aerosol filtration system that comes with standard integration of HEPA and ULPA filtration.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/surgical-technologies/products/neptune-3/images/neptune3-plus-hero-v2.png","alt":"Neptune 3"}]}],"missingAlt":[]},
