"/us/en/surgical-technologies/products/surgicount-safety-sponge-system": {"template":"product-detail","metadata":{"title":"Surgicount-Triton","pageTitle":"Surgicount-Triton","description":"Together, let's help put an end to retained surgical sponges.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/surgical-technologies/products/surgicount/images/surgicount-plus-hero.png","imageAlt":"SurgiCount","tags":["stryker:content-type/product","stryker:portfolio/medical-and-surgical-equipment","stryker:capability/sponge-management","stryker:product/surgical/surgicount-safety-sponge-system","stryker:product/surgical_technologies/Surgicount","stryker:business-unit/surgical_technologies","stryker:content-type/hcp_content"],"originallyPublished":"2023-02-06T19:53:51.000Z","lastPublished":"2026-10-08T18:49:12.000Z","contentID":"ST-GSNPS-MICRO-1161851_REV-0"},"anchors":[{"id":"overview","title":"Overview","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"features","title":"Features","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"resources","title":"Resources","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"},{"id":"contact","title":"Contact","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"customizablearea_parsys"}],"disclaimer":"<p>*Zero splash and spills, zero airborne contaminants, zero smoke, zero retained surgical sponges, zero blind spots, zero trips &amp; falls, zero drug diversion, and zero doubt messages are not guarantees and are aspirational in nature.</p>\r\n<p>Instructions for use: <a href=\"https://labeling.stryker.com/hcp/US\">https://labeling.stryker.com/hcp/US</a></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Callaghan, W. M., Creanga, A. A., &amp; Kuklina, E. V. (2012). Severe maternal morbidity among delivery and postpartum hospitalizations in the United States. Obstetrics and Gynecology, 120(5), 1029–1036. https://doi.org/10.1097/aog.0b013e31826d60c5</li>\r\n<li>Gawande, A. A., Studdert, D. M., Orav, E. J., Brennan, T. A., &amp; Zinner, M. J. (2003). Risk factors for retained instruments and sponges after surgery. The New England Journal of Medicine, 348(3), 229–235. https://doi.org/10.1056/NEJMsa021721</li>\r\n<li>Cima, R. R., Kollengode, A., Clark, J., Pool, S., Weisbrod, C., Amstutz, G. J., &amp; Deschamps, C. (2011). Using a data-matrix–coded sponge counting system across a surgical practice: Impact after 18 months. The Joint Commission Journal on Quality and Patient Safety, 37(2), 51–58. https://doi.org/10.1016/s1553-7250(11)37007-9</li>\r\n<li>Ruppel, H., Liu, V. X., Gupta, N. R., Soltesz, L., &amp; Escobar, G. J. (2021). Validation of postpartum hemorrhage admission risk factor stratification in a large obstetrics population. American Journal of Perinatology, 38(11), 1192–1200. https://doi.org/10.1055/s-0040-1712166</li>\r\n<li>Building U.S. Capacity to Review and Prevent Maternal Deaths. (2018). Report from nine maternal mortality review committees. https://www.cdcfoundation.org/sites/default/files/files/ ReportfromNineMMRCs.pdf&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ol>","forms":[{"formId":"3248","afterSubmitAction":"showMessage","message":"Thank you!","useProduction":true}],"tabs":[["Product information","Related products","Clinical research"]],"cardLists":[{"component":"featuredcontent_copy","title":null,"items":[{"path":"/us/en/surgical-technologies/products/neptune-waste-management-system","resolved":true,"title":"Neptune 3 ","description":"Neptune 3 is a constantly closed fluid, smoke, and aerosol filtration system that comes with standard integration of HEPA and ULPA filtration.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/surgical-technologies/products/neptune-3/images/neptune3-plus-hero-v2.png","alt":"Neptune 3"},{"path":"/us/en/surgical-technologies/products/safeair-compact-evacuator","resolved":false}]}],"missingAlt":[]},
