"/us/en/trauma-and-extremities/products/T2-Alpha-Humeral-Nail": {"template":"product-detail","metadata":{"title":"T2 Alpha Humeral Nail","pageTitle":"T2 Alpha Humeral Nail","description":"The T2 Alpha Humerus Nailing System offers an innovative implant that may help to improve patients' lives, simplify humeral nail fixation for surgeons and streamline processes for hospital staff.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/trauma-and-extremeties/products/t2-alpha-humeral-nail/images/T2-Alpha-Humeral-image.jpg","imageAlt":"T2-Alpha-Humeral-image","tags":["stryker:specialty/proximal-humerus","stryker:content-type/product","stryker:custom/trauma-and-extremities/product-type/nailing","stryker:capability/trauma-and-extremities","stryker:custom/trauma-and-extremities/Indications/humerus","stryker:custom/trauma-and-extremities/Procedures/Fracture","stryker:portfolio/orthopaedics","stryker:business-unit/trauma-and-extremities","stryker:content-type/hcp_content"],"originallyPublished":"2025-10-13T20:06:22.000Z","lastPublished":"2026-06-22T14:03:17.000Z","contentID":"TR-T2AL-SYK-2222877"},"anchors":[],"disclaimer":"<p>Resources:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Internal Report № D0000353370, Rev AA.</li>\r\n<li>Internal Report № D0000305724, Rev AA.</li>\r\n<li>Hoffmann S, Gerber C, et al. Effect of angular stability and other locking parameters on the mechanical performance of intramedullary nails. Biomed Tech (Berl). 2015;60(2):157-64. doi: 10.1515/bmt-2014-0100.</li>\r\n<li>Krappinger D, Bizzotto N et al. Predicting failure after surgical fixation of proximal humerus fractures. Injury. 2011;42(11):1283-8. doi: 10.1016/j.injury.2011.01.017.</li>\r\n<li>Konda SR, Maseda M, et al. Observational prospective unblinded case-control study to evaluate the effect of the Gamma3® distal targeting system for long nails on radiation exposure and time for distal screw placement, Injury. 2023;54(2):677-682. doi:10.1016/j.injury.2022.11..046</li>\r\n<li>Naidu SH, Bixler B, Capo JT, Moulton MJ, Radin A. Percutaneous pinning of proximal humerus fractures: a biomechanical study. Orthopedics. 1997;20(11):1073–6.24.</li>\r\n<li>Horn J, Gueorguiev B, Brianza S, Steen H, Schwieger K. Biomechanical evaluation of two-part surgical neck fractures of the humerus fixed by anangular stable locked intramedullary nail. J Orthop Trauma. 2011;25(7):406–13.]</li>\r\n<li>Boileau, P., d’Ollonne, T. et al. (2015). Intramedullary Nail for Proximal Humerus Fractures: An Old Concept Revisited. In: Castoldi, F., Blonna, D., Assom, M. (eds) Simple and Complex Fractures of the Humerus. Springer, Milano. doi: 10.1007/978-88-470-5307-6_8</li>\r\n<li>Internal Report № D0000379920, Rev AC</li>\r\n</ol>","forms":[],"tabs":[],"cardLists":[{"component":"customizable","title":null,"items":[{"path":"/us/en/trauma-and-extremities/products/VariAx2-Mini-Fragment-System","resolved":false},{"path":"/us/en/trauma-and-extremities/products/Pangea","resolved":true,"title":"Pangea","description":null,"image":"/content/dam/stryker/trauma-and-extremeties/products/pangea/Pangea-Plating-System-thumbnail.jpg","alt":"Pangea-Plating-System-thumbnail"},{"path":"/us/en/trauma-and-extremities/products/t2-alpha-femur-antegrade-gt-pf","resolved":true,"title":"T2 Alpha Femur Antegrade GT/PF","description":"The T2 Alpha GT/PF antegrade femoral nailing systems are intended for temporary stabilization of bone segments or fragments until bone consolidation has been achieved for femoral fractures.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/trauma-and-extremeties/images/PF-Femur-Hero-Image.png","alt":"PF-Femur-Hero-Image"},{"path":"/us/en/trauma-and-extremities/products/t2-alpha-femur-retrograde","resolved":true,"title":"T2 Alpha Femur Retrograde","description":"Stryker is a market leader in intramedullary nailing.(6) For decades, we've been creating solutions that improve treatment and set new standards. With the T2 Alpha Femur Retrograde Nailing System, surgeons have an option to treat distal and diaphyseal femoral fractures.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/trauma-and-extremeties/products/t2-alpha-femur-retrograde/images/T2-Alpha-Femur-Retrograde-main.png","alt":"retrograde femur nail, intramedullary nail, distal locking screw"}]}],"missingAlt":[]},
