"/us/en/trauma-and-extremities/products/nerve-repair": {"template":"product-detail","metadata":{"title":"Nerve repair","pageTitle":null,"description":"Our nerve portfolio consists of type I collagen conduits and wraps. They are designed to provide a protective layer around injured peripheral nerves and offer a resorbable and semi-permeable encasement to facilitate nerve repair.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/trauma-and-extremeties/products/nerve(neuroflex,neuromatrix,neuromend)/images/nerve-repair-image.png","imageAlt":null,"tags":["stryker:content-type/product","stryker:custom/trauma-and-extremities/Indications/Biologics","stryker:capability/trauma-and-extremities","stryker:custom/trauma-and-extremities/product-type/soft-tissue","stryker:custom/trauma-and-extremities/Procedures/Biologics","stryker:system/trauma-and-extremities/biologics","stryker:portfolio/orthopaedics","stryker:business-unit/trauma-and-extremities","stryker:product/trauma-and-extremities/nerve-repair","stryker:content-type/hcp_content"],"originallyPublished":null,"lastPublished":"2018-04-26T19:45:13.000Z","contentID":null},"anchors":[],"disclaimer":"<ol>\r\n<li>Li ST. Peripheral Nerve Repair with Collagen Conduits. Clinical Materials 9 (1992) 195-200.</li>\r\n<li>The results of preclinical and in vitro studies may not be indicative of human clinical outcomes<br>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Li St., Yuen D., Jenssen JR., A semipermeable, Kink Resistant Type I Colalgen-based Nerve Guide for PNS Repair. Collagen Matrix, Inc. 2003.</li>\r\n<li>U.S. Patent #6,716,225, Implant Devices for Nerve Repair, 2004.</li>\r\n<li>Taras, John, Vipul Nanavati, and Pamela Steelman. “Nerve Conduits.” Journal of Hand Therapy 18.2 (2005): 191-97.</li>\r\n<li>Weber, Robert, Warren Breidenbach, Richard Brown, Michael Jabaley, and Daniel Mass. “A Randomized Prospective Study of Polyglycolic Acid Conduits for Digital Nerve Reconstruction in Humans.” Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery 106.5 (2000): 1036-045.</li>\r\n<li>The results of preclinical and in vitro studies may not be indicative of human clinical outcomes</li>\r\n<li>Animal study data on file at Collagen Matrix, Inc</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div>Manufacturered by: Collagen Matrix, Inc. 15 Thornton Rd Oakland, NJ 07436</div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n<p>CP-AWI-12, 07-2017<br>\r\n</p>","forms":[],"tabs":[],"cardLists":[],"missingAlt":[]},
"/us/en/trauma-and-extremities/products/neuroflex": {"template":"product-detail","metadata":{"title":"Neuroflex","pageTitle":null,"description":"Nerve conduits and wraps provide an encasement for peripheral nerve injuries and protection of the neural environment. NeuroMatrix, Neuro<em>flex</em>, and NeuroMend are semi-permeable structures that allow diffusion of nutrients and neurotrophic factors into the conduit, but provide a barrier to larger, scar-forming cells.<sup>1,2</sup>","image":"/content/dam/stryker/trauma-and-extremeties/products/neuroflex/images/neuroflex-img.jpg","imageAlt":null,"tags":["stryker:product/trauma-and-extremities/neuroflex","stryker:content-type/product","stryker:custom/trauma-and-extremities/biologics/biologics-page-filters/nerve-repair-connectors","stryker:capability/biologics","stryker:specialty/nerve-repair","stryker:custom/trauma-and-extremities/biologics/nerve-repair/connectors","stryker:portfolio/orthopaedics","stryker:business-unit/trauma-and-extremities","stryker:content-type/hcp_content","stryker:capability/trauma-and-extremities"],"originallyPublished":null,"lastPublished":"2022-07-06T13:18:25.000Z","contentID":"CP-AWI-12_Rev-1, 03-2022"},"anchors":[],"disclaimer":"<ol>\r\n<li>Li ST. Peripheral Nerve Repair with Collagen Conduits. Clinical Materials 9 (1992) 195-200.</li>\r\n<li>The results of preclinical and in vitro studies may not be indicative of human clinical outcomes</li>\r\n<li>Li St., Yuen D., Jenssen JR., A semipermeable, Kink Resistant Type I Colalgen-based Nerve Guide for PNS Repair. Collagen Matrix, Inc. 2003.</li>\r\n<li>U.S. Patent #6,716,225, Implant Devices for Nerve Repair, 2004.</li>\r\n<li>Taras, John, Vipul Nanavati, and Pamela Steelman. “Nerve Conduits.” Journal of Hand Therapy 18.2 (2005): 191-97.</li>\r\n<li>Weber, Robert, Warren Breidenbach, Richard Brown, Michael Jabaley, and Daniel Mass. “A Randomized Prospective Study of Polyglycolic Acid Conduits for Digital Nerve Reconstruction in Humans.” Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery 106.5 (2000): 1036-045.</li>\r\n<li>The results of preclinical and in vitro studies may not be indicative of human clinical outcomes</li>\r\n<li>Animal study data on file at Collagen Matrix, Inc</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div>Manufacturered&nbsp;by: Collagen Matrix, Inc. 15 Thornton Rd Oakland, NJ 07436</div>","forms":[],"tabs":[],"cardLists":[],"missingAlt":[]},
